  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Healthcare Disease Prediction — Duplicate & Irrelevant Column Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "The objective of this notebook is to identify duplicate records and evaluate whether any columns are irrelevant or unsuitable for disease prediction.\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook focuses on analysis and documentation. Final data cleaning and feature selection will be performed in the appropriate preprocessing stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Import required libraries\n",
        "\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Libraries imported successfully.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Load the Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset is loaded directly from the Team-6 GitHub repository."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# GitHub raw dataset URL\n",
        "\n",
        "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vyasanbmathew2008/Team-6/main/healthcare-disease-prediction/dataset/healthcare_dataset.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load dataset\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Dataset loaded successfully!\")\n",
        "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display first 5 records\n",
        "\n",
        "display(df.head())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Identify Duplicate Records\n",
        "\n",
        "Duplicate records are rows containing the same disease and symptom information. These records can give excessive weight to particular disease-symptom combinations and should be examined before model training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Count exact duplicate records\n",
        "\n",
        "duplicate_count = df.duplicated().sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Number of exact duplicate records:\", duplicate_count)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Calculate duplicate percentage\n",
        "\n",
        "duplicate_percentage = (duplicate_count / len(df)) * 100\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Duplicate percentage: {duplicate_percentage:.2f}%\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display duplicate records\n",
        "\n",
        "duplicate_records = df[df.duplicated(keep=False)]\n        \n",
        "print(\"Duplicate records:\")\n",
        "display(duplicate_records.head(20))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Check Duplicate Disease-Symptom Combinations\n",
        "\n",
        "Exact duplicate rows are not the only type of duplication. The same disease with the same symptoms may appear more than once even when the rows differ in formatting or other fields."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Identify disease and symptom columns\n",
        "\n",
        "symptom_columns = [\n",
        "    column for column in df.columns\n",
        "    if column.lower().startswith(\"symptom\")\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "target_column = \"Disease\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Target column:\", target_column)\n",
        "print(\"Symptom columns:\")\n",
        "print(symptom_columns)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Check duplicate disease-symptom combinations\n",
        "\n",
        "disease_symptom_columns = [target_column] + symptom_columns\n",
        "\n",
        "disease_symptom_duplicates = df.duplicated(\n",
        "    subset=disease_symptom_columns,\n",
        "    keep=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "duplicate_disease_symptom_count = disease_symptom_duplicates.sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Duplicate disease-symptom records:\", duplicate_disease_symptom_count)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display duplicate disease-symptom combinations\n",
        "\n",
        "display(\n",
        "    df.loc[disease_symptom_duplicates, disease_symptom_columns].head(20)\n",
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Analyze Column Characteristics\n",
        "\n",
        "Each column is examined using its data type and number of unique values. A high number of unique values does not automatically mean that a column is irrelevant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display columns, data types, unique values and unique percentage\n",
        "\n",
        "column_analysis = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Column\": df.columns,\n",
        "    \"Data Type\": df.dtypes.astype(str).values,\n",
        "    \"Unique Values\": [\n",
        "        df[column].nunique(dropna=True)\n",
        "        for column in df.columns\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "    \"Unique Percentage\": [\n",
        "        (df[column].nunique(dropna=True) / len(df)) * 100\n",
        "        for column in df.columns\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "column_analysis[\"Unique Percentage\"] = column_analysis[\"Unique Percentage\"].round(2)\n",
        "\n",
        "display(column_analysis)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Identify Constant and Near-Constant Columns\n",
        "\n",
        "Columns containing only one unique value do not provide useful information for machine learning. Such columns can be considered for removal during preprocessing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Find constant columns\n",
        "\n",
        "constant_columns = [\n",
        "    column for column in df.columns\n",
        "    if df[column].nunique(dropna=False) <= 1\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Constant columns:\")\n",
        "print(constant_columns if constant_columns else \"None\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Check highly repetitive columns\n",
        "\n",
        "near_constant_columns = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for column in df.columns:\n",
        "    top_frequency = df[column].value_counts(dropna=False, normalize=True).iloc[0]\n",
        "    if top_frequency >= 0.99:\n",
        "        near_constant_columns.append(column)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Near-constant columns (99% or more same value):\")\n",
        "print(near_constant_columns if near_constant_columns else \"None\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Identify Potentially Irrelevant Columns\n",
        "\n",
        "For this disease prediction dataset, the disease column is the target variable and the symptom columns are the primary predictive features.\n",
        "\n",
        "Columns are evaluated based on whether they provide useful information for disease prediction, whether they are identifiers, and whether they create unnecessary complexity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Identify columns that are not the target or symptom features\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_columns = [\n",
        "    column for column in df.columns\n",
        "    if column != target_column and column not in symptom_columns\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Columns outside the Disease and Symptom features:\")\n",
        "print(feature_columns if feature_columns else \"None\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Initial Feature Relevance Review\n",
        "\n",
        "| Column Type | Assessment | Reason |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Disease | Target | This is the disease class that the model will predict. |\n",
        "| Symptom_1 to Symptom_n | Relevant | Symptoms are the main input features for disease prediction. |\n",
        "| Constant columns | Irrelevant | A column with one value provides no predictive information. |\n",
        "| Identifier columns | Potentially irrelevant | Identifiers generally do not describe disease characteristics. |\n",
        "| Administrative columns | Potentially irrelevant | Administrative information may not improve symptom-based disease prediction. |\n",
        "\n",
        "> These are initial assessments. Final feature removal should be performed during the data cleaning and preprocessing stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Check Target Variable Distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "The disease column is treated as the target variable. Its distribution is checked to understand the number of disease classes and the number of records belonging to each class."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"Target variable:\", target_column)\n",
        "print(\"Number of disease classes:\", df[target_column].nunique())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nDisease categories:\")\n",
        "print(df[target_column].unique())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Disease frequency\n",
        "\n",
        "disease_counts = df[target_column].value_counts()\n",
        "\n",
        "display(disease_counts.to_frame(\"Record Count\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Plot disease distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "sns.countplot(data=df, x=target_column, order=disease_counts.index)\n",
        "plt.title(\"Distribution of Diseases\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Disease\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Number of Records\")\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=90)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Check Duplicate Disease Counts\n",
        "\n",
        "This section checks how many records are available for each disease. This is useful for identifying diseases with unusually high or low representation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "disease_duplicate_summary = df.groupby(target_column).size().reset_index(name=\"Record Count\")\n",
        "disease_duplicate_summary = disease_duplicate_summary.sort_values(\n",
        "    \"Record Count\", ascending=False\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "display(disease_duplicate_summary)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Duplicate and Irrelevant Column Summary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "print(\"DUPLICATE & IRRELEVANT COLUMN ANALYSIS\")\n",
        "print(\"=\" * 55)\n        \n        "print(f\"Total records             : {len(df)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Total columns             : {len(df.columns)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Exact duplicate records   : {duplicate_count}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Duplicate percentage      : {duplicate_percentage:.2f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"Disease-symptom duplicates: {duplicate_disease_symptom_count}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Target variable           : {target_column}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Number of disease classes : {df[target_column].nunique()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Symptom columns           : {len(symptom_columns)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Constant columns          : {len(constant_columns)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 10. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "- Exact duplicate records were identified.\n",
        "- Duplicate disease-symptom combinations were examined.\n",
        "- Column data types and unique-value counts were analyzed.\n",
        "- Constant and near-constant columns were checked.\n",
        "- The Disease column was identified as the target variable.\n",
        "- Symptom columns were identified as the main predictive features.\n",
        "- Potentially irrelevant columns were identified for further review.\n",
        "- No records or columns are removed in this analysis notebook.\n",
        "- Final removal and preprocessing decisions will be performed in the next data-cleaning stage."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
